ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Looks good to me on principle, but I don't have a microphone with more than 2 channels to test this.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#pullrequestreview-2595065353","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101673","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#pullrequestreview-2595065353"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101673"}},"submitted_at":"2025-02-05T09:15:05Z","commit_id":"ab67c47c8d63553ff634617917f73642b5276a6c"},{"id":4881947630,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIvyb7g","user":{"login":"Jaytheway","id":22476284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDc2Mjg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22476284?u=02d933b530b26d757decb436944bf86bbcb046b2&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway","html_url":"https://github.com/Jaytheway","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"None of the audio backends implemented in Godot seem to support more than 2 channel input audio devices. Some seem to handle it silently (like CoreAudio), others print a warning (like PulseAudio).\r\n\r\nI'd argue that for consistency sake, either all backends should be extended, or only the fist two channels should be used in all.\r\nBut generally silently mixing input channels together under the hood is likely not a good idea. If other channels of an input device serve other purpose than traditional microphone input, e.g. if they represent noise cancellation microphones - when mixed with the intended first two channels, may produce unexpected results.\r\n\r\nIf there's no consensus on the above mentioned, the code looks fine, technically addresses the issue, just minor errors as I pointed out in the review comments.\r\nHowever, I was unable to test and verify the fix on my setup.\r\n\r\nWorth pointing out, the original issue was \"Godot does not listen to microphones with over 2 channels\", while the PR adds new behavior of \"downmixing all the extra input channels to 2\" and technically Godot still doesn't provide more than 2 channels of input audio to the user after this PR.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#pullrequestreview-4881947630","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101673","author_association":"NONE","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101673#pullrequestreview-4881947630"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101673"}},"submitted_at":"2026-08-07T10:50:48Z","commit_id":"a06c4b4e4bd4fc8f807612a6675767695c3b7054"},{"id":4882320788,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIwJNlA","user":{"login":"Jaytheway","id":22476284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDc2Mjg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22476284?u=02d933b530b26d757decb436944bf86bbcb046b2&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway","html_url":"https://github.com/Jaytheway","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jaytheway/fo